  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A rectangle has dimensions $x\\text{ cm}\\times y\\text{ cm}$ where $x$ and $y$ are integers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Given the area of the rectangle is $40\\text{ cm}^2$, find the smallest perimeter that the rectangle can have.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$26\\text{ cm}$.\n\nCompare the integer factor pairs of $40$; $5\\times8$ gives the smallest perimeter.",
          "worked": "The positive integer side pairs, ignoring reversed pairs, are $(1,40)$, $(2,20)$, $(4,10)$ and $(5,8)$.\n\nTheir perimeters are $82$, $44$, $28$ and $26\\text{ cm}$ respectively. Thus the minimum occurs for $5\\text{ cm}\\times8\\text{ cm}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=2(5+8)\\\\P&=26\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Given the perimeter of the rectangle is $20\\text{ cm}$, find the largest area that the rectangle can have.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$25\\text{ cm}^2$.\n\nCompare the positive integer side pairs with sum $10$; $5\\times5$ gives the largest area.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=\\frac{20}{2}\\\\x+y&=10.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe positive integer side pairs, ignoring reversed pairs, are $(1,9)$, $(2,8)$, $(3,7)$, $(4,6)$ and $(5,5)$. Their areas are $9$, $16$, $21$, $24$ and $25\\text{ cm}^2$ respectively.\n\nThe largest area is $25\\text{ cm}^2$, for a $5\\text{ cm}\\times5\\text{ cm}$ rectangle.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
